WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.294
Part one.

00:00:01.294 --> 00:00:03.376
Record a test in one click.

00:00:04.833 --> 00:00:07.718
This is Demo Books, a small online bookstore.

00:00:07.718 --> 00:00:13.820
Today we'll test its checkout, from picking a book to placing the order, without writing a single line of code.

00:00:13.833 --> 00:00:16.428
Pocket QA sits right in the browser toolbar.

00:00:16.428 --> 00:00:18.283
Click its icon to open it.

00:00:18.967 --> 00:00:23.849
On a new tab it starts switched off, so it never touches a page until you say so.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.472
Click Start Recording.

00:00:25.472 --> 00:00:28.150
Pocket QA asks to turn on for this tab.

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:29.418
Choose Turn on.

00:00:29.433 --> 00:00:34.835
The popup closes, a red Recording bar appears on the page, and the toolbar badge says REC.

00:00:34.835 --> 00:00:37.727
From now on, everything you do is captured.

00:00:37.733 --> 00:00:43.796
The bar also has a ✓ Check button: with it, or Alt and a click, whatever you point at becomes a check.

00:00:43.796 --> 00:00:46.012
We'll add our first check in part three.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:53.486
First, click Books in the menu, so the test always starts from the book list, whatever page you are on when it runs.

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.255
Sort the books by price,

00:00:56.567 --> 00:00:58.959
then sign in like a regular customer.

00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:07.576
Add a book to the cart.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:14.549
Open the cart, check out, fill in the name and address, pick express shipping, and place the order.

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:22.533
The order is confirmed.

00:01:22.533 --> 00:01:24.620
Click Stop right on the Recording bar.

00:01:26.433 --> 00:01:28.193
Open Pocket QA again.

00:01:28.193 --> 00:01:32.082
Each action is now a step, named after the element it touched.

00:01:32.082 --> 00:01:34.232
No selectors to write by hand.

00:01:34.233 --> 00:01:37.005
Name the scenario Buy a book, and save it.

00:01:39.167 --> 00:01:41.280
A recorder only sees what you did.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:45.281
Say we want a second book in the cart: we can add that step by hand.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.902
The plus sign between two steps picks where the new one goes.

00:01:48.902 --> 00:01:51.033
We choose right after the first book.

00:01:51.033 --> 00:01:56.862
Choose Click, hit the target button, then point straight at another book's Add to cart button on the page.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:06.753
The popup opens again with the selector filled in, plus fallback locators.

00:02:06.753 --> 00:02:10.067
Hover the eye icon to see the element outlined on the page.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.727
Give it a clear name and click Add Action.

00:02:12.727 --> 00:02:15.521
The new step lands exactly where we chose.

00:02:18.167 --> 00:02:19.320
Changed your mind?

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:25.278
Undo and Redo go back up to fifty steps, and every edit is saved straight into the scenario.

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:27.225
Our first scenario is ready.

00:02:27.225 --> 00:02:29.834
Next, let's watch it play back on its own.
